  "text": " So first of all, I am not anti-vaccine. Right, right, right. I am not anti-FDA. I am not conspiracy theorist. I have no history of any of this prior to my finding out about what happened with these vaccines. Right. So and in fact, just to prove that I'm doubly vaccinated, my kids are doubly vaccinated. Wow. My wife is doubly vaccinated. Wow. And that was all done before the end of March. I've gone 180. Yeah. So what made the shift is that I got a message, I'd get a DM on Twitter. OK. And it was from somebody I didn't know at the time. And she said, she asked me, are the vaccines safe? And I said, of course they're safe. You know, the FDA says they're like, I've got everything under a magnifying glass. And this is the safest vaccine ever. And it's safe and effective. And nobody has died. And how could you even ask such a dumb question like that? I mean, I kind of had that attitude. And so she answers. She says, well, three of my relatives who were healthy got the jab and they died a week later. OK. So I'm going like, yeah, yeah, sure. Right. Don't really know this person. So I'm writing it off. So then a week later, my carpet cleaner comes in, Tim Damroff. And Tim's wearing a mask. And so I'm giving him a hard time. I said, Tim, didn't you get the memo? You're supposed to get the vaccine. You don't have to wear a mask after you get the vaccine. Right. Steve, I did get the vaccine. But I had a side effect. And I can't get the second dose. I said, what happened? And he said, well, I had a heart attack two minutes after I got the shot. And so this guy has been in pain ever since then. Oh my gosh. Ever since that time. And he has extreme difficulty in working and getting through the day. Oh my gosh. And then he told me that his wife, he showed me a video of his wife. His wife has Parkinson's disease where she holds up a cup and she can't hold it steady. Yes, I've seen it. And it's only in the arm, the injection arm. Oh, what a coincidence.",
